# What Docker may send to the build. This is NOT what keeps private files out
# of the image: the Dockerfile copies only the files named in
# docker-build-files.txt (made from `git ls-files`). This list just keeps the
# upload small and leaves out things no build needs (git history, local
# installs and builds, hidden files, tests). Everything the list names must be
# allowed here, or the build stops and says which file is missing.
*

!docker-build-files.txt
!scripts/docker-copy-inputs.sh
!docker-entrypoint.sh

!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!scripts/copy-assets.mjs
!examples/serve.mjs
!packages/*/package.json
!packages/*/tsconfig.json
!packages/*/src/**

# Each folder is named twice: once for the folder and once (with /**) for
# everything inside it, or the "!" lines above would let its files back in.
**/__tests__
**/__tests__/**
**/.*
**/.*/**
**/node_modules
**/node_modules/**
**/dist
**/dist/**
